    "created_at": "2015-09-24T06:34:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-24T06:34:29Z",
    "body": "I really am not worried about that personally, since you can't run script that accesses `location` until script is loaded, so the intermediate state is not observable.\n\nIf you make the change to having a WorkerGlobalScope, then _maybe_ I'd think of inserting a note like \"This WorkerLocation's associated WorkerGlobalScope will only have its url property set after the worker script has been fetched. This does not impact the above algorithms, since these getters can only run after script has been fetched.\"\n",
